Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The supplied code contains the diagnosis module, not the HSTU implementation. It
inspects item embeddings through `view.item_emb` and sequence features through 
`view.log2feats(sequence)`. The actual trained network is `view.model`; its 
`itemnum` bounds the item embedding slice.

The probe scores features at every valid training position. It does not 
explicitly extract a final user representation. The backbone’s feature 
computation and final-position readout cannot be verified from this code; 
left-padded histories require the final nonpadding position.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` receives the compatibility wrapper and stores its
`meta_data`, `review_data`, and `user_train`. Only metadata is subsequently used
directly.

The loader supplies `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with tensors shaped 
`B × L`. Sequences pass through `log2feats`; positive and negative IDs are 
stacked into `B × L × 2` and scored using `predict_score(features, items)`. 
Positions with positive ID zero are excluded. Scoring runs in evaluation mode 
without gradients.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse:** Samples up to 2,048 real-item embeddings using seed 
42, excluding padding and reserved tokens. It normalizes vectors, averages 
off-diagonal cosine similarities, and maps the result to `[0,1]`. Higher values 
suggest directional collapse; orthogonal embeddings yield approximately 0.5.
- **Positive–negative separation:** Processes up to ten batches and computes 
positive minus negative logits. Higher mean and 10th-percentile margins indicate
stronger separation. Lower negative-wins and small-margin rates are preferable; 
the small-margin threshold is 0.5.
- **Category breakdown:** Counts category occurrences separately for positive 
and negative items in low-margin and wrong-ranking cases, retaining the top 20 
categories.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence perturbation, shuffling, ablation, or sensitivity test is 
implemented. Random embedding sampling only limits computational cost.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, covering 
collapse, four margin statistics, and nested category counts. 
`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds these into a prompt requesting status, 
core findings, implications, and supporting evidence; it does not itself 
generate that interpretation.

These are training-sample diagnostics, not validation HR@10. Margins depend on 
score scale and sampled negatives. Available task metadata excludes item 
categories, so category counts will be empty. Reviews and stored histories are 
unused. Empty margin samples produce zeros, potentially obscuring missing 
evidence. The probes do not assess temporal sensitivity, generalization, 
recommendation coverage, or gradient health.

