Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The supplied file diagnoses item embeddings and sequence-conditioned ranking 
scores; it does not include the HSTU backbone implementation. 
`log2feats(sequence)` supplies per-position sequence features, and 
`predict_score(features, items)` scores candidate items. The probes evaluate all
valid target positions rather than extracting a final user representation. Final
inference readout cannot be verified here; left-padded histories require the 
final nonpadding position.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` stores the compatibility view, although the 
constructor names it `model`. It accesses `item_emb`, `log2feats`, 
`predict_score`, and the underlying model’s `itemnum` through that view. It also
stores `meta_data`, `review_data`, and `user_train`; the latter two are unused.

`run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` examines up to ten batches of `(None, 
sequence, positive, negative)`, with tensors shaped B × L. Ranking analysis runs
in evaluation mode without gradients and excludes positions whose positive 
target is padding (`0`).

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse:** Samples up to 2,048 real item embeddings using seed 
42, excluding padding and reserved tokens. It normalizes vectors, averages 
off-diagonal cosine similarities, and maps the result to [0,1]. Higher values 
indicate stronger directional alignment; approximately 0.5 corresponds to zero 
mean cosine similarity.
- **Positive–negative separation:** Scores each supplied positive and negative 
at each position, then computes their logit difference. Outputs include the 
mean, tenth percentile, fraction below zero, and fraction below 0.5. Larger 
margins and smaller failure fractions indicate stronger sampled ranking 
separation.
- **Category breakdown:** Counts positive and negative item category occurrences
among weak-margin and incorrectly ranked positions, retaining the top twenty 
categories separately.

# Perturbation & Tests

There are no sequence perturbations, shuffle tests, ablations, or sensitivity 
checks. Random sampling only selects embeddings; negative candidates come from 
the loader.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

The result contains `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. Metric keys are 
`embedding_collapse_score`, `pos_neg_margin_mean`, `pos_neg_margin_p10`, 
`pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate`, `pos_neg_small_margin_rate`, and 
`pos_neg_margin_category_breakdown`.

`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds both dictionaries into a prompt requesting
an evidence-grounded JSON interpretation.

These training-sample probes do not measure validation HR@10, generalization, 
gradients, or recommendation diversity directly. Category metadata is 
unavailable in this task, so category lists should remain empty. Empty margin 
samples produce zeros that must not be mistaken for healthy measurements.

