Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The supplied module diagnoses one fitted HSTU model per category. It accesses 
effective item embeddings through `item_emb`, causal sequence features through 
`log2feats(sequence)`, and aligned or candidate scores through 
`predict_score(features, items)`. Inputs contain item IDs and learned absolute 
positions. For left-padded histories, the final representation comes from the 
greatest nonpadding index, never `count-1`. Backbone implementation details are 
not supplied.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` receives the host ModelView; `view.model` is the 
actual network. It reads catalog size, maximum sequence length, category 
identity, and `user_train['History']`. Loader batches provide `(None, sequence, 
positive, negative)` with matching B × L tensors; shapes and item IDs are 
validated.

`run_full_diagnosis` caches at most ten batches, enables evaluation/inference 
mode, and restores module modes and captured random-generator states afterward.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse:** Samples up to 2,048 item embeddings and rescales their
mean off-diagonal cosine to [0,1]. Approximately 0.5 means zero mean cosine; 
values near 1 indicate strong angular alignment. This does not measure 
representation rank or recommendation diversity.
- **Positive–negative margins:** Reports mean margin, tenth percentile, 
negative-wins rate, and fraction below 0.5 over valid training positions. Larger
margins and fewer ranking errors generally indicate stronger sampled-pair 
separation; the threshold depends on score scale.
- **History audit:** Reports original rank, reciprocal rank, and hit@10, plus 
paired intervention effects. Lower rank and higher reciprocal rank/hit@10 
indicate better target placement.
- **Cost:** Records wall time, CUDA interval, peak allocation, and scoring 
counts.

# Perturbation & Tests

Up to 32 training users contribute two prefixes each; loader rows provide a 
fallback. Each prefix shares one target and up to 999 unique negatives across 
variants. Tests remove recent, oldest, final, or prefinal events, and average 
three nonfinal shuffles. Deletions compact histories and restore left padding. 
Effects measure frozen-model sensitivity; user-cluster bootstrapping supplies 
conditional intervals when identities permit.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

Output contains `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, including coverage, 
exclusions, effects, uncertainty, and null reasons. Unavailable category 
breakdowns and four-category macro estimates remain empty/null. These training 
diagnostics do not establish validation performance, generalization, intent, 
elapsed-time effects, diversity, or conformity. The interpreter prompt requests 
a grounded JSON status, findings, implications, and evidence.

