Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The supplied code contains only the diagnosis module; HSTU internals and final 
sequence readout cannot be verified. Diagnosis accesses item embeddings through 
`view.item_emb.weight`, sequence features through `view.log2feats(sequence)`, 
and candidate logits through `view.predict_score(features, items)`. Margin 
analysis uses features at valid training positions rather than explicitly 
selecting a final user representation. Any final readout must respect left 
padding and use the final nonpadding position.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` stores the compatibility view (named `model` in 
the constructor), including `meta_data`, `review_data`, and `user_train`; the 
latter two are unused. The underlying trained module is accessible as 
`view.model`.

`run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` examines up to ten batches of `(None, 
sequence, positive, negative)`, each with tensors shaped `B × L`. It switches 
the view to evaluation mode, computes sequence features, stacks 
positive/negative IDs into `B × L × 2`, and scores them. Positions with positive
ID zero are excluded.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse:** Samples at most 2,048 real-item embeddings using seed 
42, excluding padding and reserved tokens. It normalizes embeddings, averages 
off-diagonal cosine similarities, and maps the result to `[0,1]`. Higher values 
suggest directional collapse; approximately 0.5 corresponds to zero average 
cosine similarity.
- **Positive–negative separation:** Computes `positive_logit − negative_logit`. 
Higher mean and 10th-percentile margins indicate stronger separation. Lower 
negative-beats-positive and small-margin rates are preferable; the small-margin 
threshold is 0.5.
- **Category breakdown:** Counts positive and negative item categories 
separately for weak-margin and incorrect rankings, returning the top 20 
categories by count.

# Perturbation & Tests

No histories are shuffled, masked, reordered, or otherwise perturbed. Random 
embedding subsampling estimates geometry; it does not test behavioral 
sensitivity. Margin probes assess supplied training negatives only.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

The returned dictionary contains `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, covering 
collapse, four margin statistics, and category breakdowns with thresholds and 
position totals. `diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds both into a prompt 
requesting a grounded JSON interpretation.

These probes do not measure validation HR@10, generalization, sequence 
sensitivity, or user-level recommendation diversity. Categories are unavailable 
under this benchmark, so category lists should remain empty. Missing valid 
positions produce zero margin statistics, which must not be interpreted as 
healthy performance.

